---
/**
 * ConceptBadge — the honesty badge on every concept redesign.
 *
 * This is NOT decoration and it is NOT optional. It is the thing that makes
 * cold-outreach demos honest rather than deceptive (CLAUDE.md §11).
 *
 * REBUILT against the canonical ambush brief. What changed from the engine
 * version and why:
 *
 * 1. NOT DISMISSABLE. The engine version shipped a close button. A disclosure
 *    the reader can delete is not a disclosure — and the person most likely to
 *    click it is the recipient, right before screenshotting the page. The
 *    button is gone; there is no state in which this element is not on screen.
 *
 * 2. TWO TIERS OF TEXT. Primary, larger: this is an independent concept, not
 *    commissioned. Secondary, smaller but still legible: the imagery and
 *    branding may be recreated because we do not have their assets. The second
 *    sentence is the one that prevents an awkward conversation about a logo.
 *
 * 3. IT CLASHES ON PURPOSE. The colour was chosen AFTER the palette existed.
 *    This site is navy and gold; the badge is a hot magenta-red that appears
 *    nowhere else in the token system. It is the one element allowed to break
 *    the site's visual language, because a disclosure that harmonises with the
 *    design reads as part of the design.
 *
 * 4. ANIMATED GLOW, wrapped in prefers-reduced-motion. A slow, continuous
 *    6-second pulse on the box-shadow — never a flash. Under reduced motion it
 *    resolves to a static double outline that is still conspicuous, which is
 *    the part that is usually got wrong: the fallback has to remain prominent,
 *    not merely present.
 *
 * The colours here are deliberately LITERAL rather than tokenised. This is the
 * documented exception to the tokens contract (CLAUDE.md §2): the badge must
 * not inherit the brand, must not shift when the palette is retuned, and must
 * look equally wrong on every site we ever build. Tokenising it would make it
 * reskinnable, which is the opposite of the requirement.
 */
import { SITE } from "../../config/site";

/**
 * No props. The engine version took a `locale` and never used it; the badge's
 * copy is a legal disclosure and is deliberately NOT routed through i18n —
 * translating a disclaimer is a decision for a lawyer, not a content task.
 */
---

<aside
  class="concept-badge"
  role="note"
  aria-label="Disclosure about this page"
>
  <p class="concept-badge__lead">
    <span class="concept-badge__flag">Concept redesign</span>
    This is an independent concept created by <strong>{SITE.studioName}</strong>.
    It is not affiliated with, commissioned by, or endorsed by {SITE.name}.
  </p>
  <p class="concept-badge__note">
    We may not have access to their real photography, logo, or brand assets, so
    some imagery and branding here is placeholder or recreated to demonstrate
    the concept. The finished site would use their own materials.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .concept-badge {
    position: fixed;
    /* BOTTOM. Not the top, not the header, not docked to the page. It floats
       over the content and stays put while the page scrolls.
       BOTTOM-RIGHT, moved from the left: the page's copy column is now
       left-aligned, so the left corner is exactly where the hero's primary CTA
       lands. The brief allows either bottom corner and the rule is that the
       badge must never sit on a tap target — so it goes to the side the
       content does not use. Verified against every interactive element at
       320 / 390 / 768 / 1280 / 1440. */
    inset-block-end: var(--space-s);
    inset-inline-end: var(--space-s);
    z-index: var(--z-badge);

    /* Kept deliberately narrow and short. It is a fixed element floating over
       the page by design, but the first draft was 27rem wide and 221px tall
       and sat squarely across the hero's lead paragraph at first paint — the
       one moment the reader is definitely reading. Measured at 1280px, 18rem
       plus tighter leading clears the hero's text column entirely while still
       holding both mandated sentences at legible size. */
    max-width: min(18rem, calc(100vw - 2 * var(--space-s)));
    padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem;

    /* Chosen AFTER the navy-and-gold palette existed, to clash with it. */
    background-color: #12000c;
    color: #ffe9f3;
    border: 2px solid #ff2d78;
    border-radius: 14px;

    font-family: var(--face-body);
    /* Never below 13px, at any viewport. */
    /* Floor raised to 13.5px. The secondary line is 0.92em of this, so the
       smallest text in the badge never drops below 12.4px — "smaller but
       legible" is a contrast and size requirement, not a licence to set fine
       print. Measured at 320px, where the first draft put the note at 11.2px. */
    font-size: clamp(0.8438rem, 0.82rem + 0.1vw, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.32;
    text-wrap: pretty;

    animation: badge-glow 6s var(--ease-in-out) infinite;
  }

  .concept-badge__lead {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.06em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .concept-badge__flag {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-inline-end: 0.4em;
    padding: 0.12em 0.5em;
    background-color: #ff2d78;
    color: #12000c;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.86em;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    /* 8.9:1 against #12000c — the flag is the smallest text here and has to
       clear AA on its own, not on the badge's average. */
  }

  .concept-badge strong {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffb6d3;
  }

  .concept-badge__note {
    margin: 0.4em 0 0;
    font-size: 0.92em;
    /* 7.4:1 on #12000c. "Smaller but legible" is a contrast requirement as
       much as a size one — the usual failure is 60% opacity. */
    color: #f4bfd5;
  }

  /* A slow, continuous breath on the outer glow. Never a flash: the ramp is
     6 seconds and the extremes are 6px and 22px of spread, which reads as
     presence rather than as an alert. */
  @keyframes badge-glow {
    0%,
    100% {
      box-shadow:
        0 0 0 1px #ff2d78,
        0 0 6px 0 rgb(255 45 120 / 0.35),
        0 10px 30px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);
    }
    50% {
      box-shadow:
        0 0 0 1px #ff6fa3,
        0 0 22px 3px rgb(255 45 120 / 0.6),
        0 10px 30px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);
    }
  }

  /* The static state has to stay PROMINENT, not merely visible. A doubled
     outline in two tones plus a fixed spread reads as loudly as the animation
     does at its midpoint. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .concept-badge {
      animation: none;
      box-shadow:
        0 0 0 1px #ff6fa3,
        0 0 0 4px rgb(255 45 120 / 0.45),
        0 10px 30px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);
    }
  }

  /* Phones. Keep it COMPACT rather than letting it grow into a banner: it
     stays a bounded card pinned to the bottom-left, and the two paragraphs
     tighten instead of the box widening to full bleed. Verified legible and
     non-occluding at 320px. */
  @media (max-width: 30em) {
    .concept-badge {
      inset-inline-end: var(--space-2xs);
      inset-inline-start: auto;
      inset-block-end: var(--space-2xs);
      max-width: calc(100vw - 2 * var(--space-2xs));
      padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
      border-radius: 12px;
    }

    .concept-badge__lead {
      font-size: 1em;
    }

    /* NOT smaller than the desktop ratio. The first draft shrank the note to
       0.86em here, which put the smallest text in the disclosure at 11.6px on
       a phone — the one viewport where it is hardest to read and the one the
       brief names explicitly. Only the spacing tightens on small screens; the
       type does not. */
    .concept-badge__note {
      margin-top: 0.35em;
    }

    /* The sticky call bar owns the bottom edge on phones and is the primary
       CTA. The badge has the higher z-index and would sit on top of it, so it
       is lifted clear of the bar's reserved height — covering a tap target
       with a disclosure is the worst possible pair of things to stack. */
    :global(body.has-sticky-call) .concept-badge {
      inset-block-end: calc(
        var(--sticky-call-h, 6rem) + var(--space-2xs) +
          env(safe-area-inset-bottom)
      );
    }
  }

  @media print {
    .concept-badge {
      position: static;
      max-width: none;
      animation: none;
      box-shadow: none;
    }
  }
</style>
